# What this board does not work without, on top of common/kernel.required.
# The panel's own drivers are in the panel's file.

MMC_BLOCK                 the card as a block device, which the exchange partition is mounted from
SERIAL_AMBA_PL011_CONSOLE the PL011 on the GPIO header, the only console in the release image
BCM2835_MBOX              the mailbox the framebuffer and the firmware driver run on
RASPBERRYPI_FIRMWARE      the in-kernel firmware interface; clocks, power domains and the framebuffer all go through it
RASPBERRYPI_POWER         the firmware power domains; the USB controller and the camera are behind them
BCM2835_WDT               poweroff: this driver owns pm_power_off on a Pi, so the board does not power down without it
DMA_BCM2835               the DMA channel that feeds the DPI panel
PINCTRL_BCM2835           the pin multiplexing every other on-SoC driver depends on
VIDEO_BCM2835             the legacy camera: the GPU runs the sensor and this publishes it as V4L2
BCM2835_VCHIQ_MMAL        the transport VIDEO_BCM2835 talks to the GPU over

CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_SCHEDUTIL the Pi defconfig's default governor is powersave, which holds the cores at their lowest clock

# Faraday (docs/history/PLAN.md §4.3).
MSDOS_PARTITION           the card's partitions as their own nodes, so the whole card is never handed out

# The display, input and storage (docs/IMAGES.md §1). The screen's own driver is the panel's.

DRM                    the kernel-mode-setting stack a screen behind HDMI or DSI is driven through
DRM_VC4                vc4's display side: the HVS, the pixel valves and the HDMI and DSI encoders; its V3D binds too, and its render node is root's (F153)
DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION    /dev/fb0 over DRM, which is what the shell writes every frame to
HID                    a USB keyboard, mouse and touchscreen are all HIDs
HID_GENERIC            USB keyboards and mice
USB_HID                the transport they arrive on
HID_MULTITOUCH         what a USB touchscreen reports through
USB_STORAGE            a USB stick, whose partitions reach the disk process through faraday-grant
SCSI                   the layer USB storage hands its disk to
BLK_DEV_SD             that disk as /dev/sdX
EFI_PARTITION          most sticks are GPT; without the parser there is no partition to hand out
